        "task": "Audit PII leakage in public/unauthenticated endpoints of /workspace/server (call get_threat_model target /workspace/server first).\n\nSHELL QUIRK: exec_command default pipes swallow output — always pass tty:true.\n\nCONTEXT: LGPD health app. Sensitive: CPF (encrypted+masked helpers exist), patient photos (facial), exam PDFs/lab results, clinical narratives, mental-health screenings. Public surface: /api/public/* (decifre, lead, v1 API, shared reports w/ token+6-digit PIN), /api/labs, /api/doctor/crm, /api/consulta, /api/patients/:id/photo (any-valid-JWT ?t=), /api/health, /api/app/*, /api/docs (swagger), /api/auth/*.\n\nDO:\n1. Map every route mounted BEFORE requireAuth or on public routers (app.ts + each routes file's own guard usage). Build the full unauthenticated-endpoint inventory.\n2. For each: what data does it return? Trace prisma selects — do any include cpfEncrypted/cpfLast4/fullName/birthDate/email/health data without auth? Check public-api.routes.ts (v1 API — API-key middleware? what PII?), decifre.routes.ts, lead.routes.ts (lead capture storing PII publicly?), labs.routes.ts, consulta.ts.\n3. Shared exam reports: /api/public/shared/:token (+PIN) — analyze token entropy (how generated? JWT? random?), PIN brute-force economics vs the 10/15min limiter, share-pin hashing (utils/crypto hashSharePin), what fields the shared view exposes (full CPF? photos? items?), and whether token can enumerate other patients' shares. Check doctor-share.routes.ts public access paths.\n4. /api/patients/:id/photo requirePhotoToken: accepts ANY valid JWT (patient or doctor) for ANY patient id. Assess: is the CUID guessable/leakable elsewhere (do any endpoints return other users' patient CUIDs — e.g. labs, shared reports, errors, logs)? If an attacker can obtain victim CUIDs, they get facial photos (LGPD biometric). Cross-check with BOLA findings note if present.\n5. Error messages: errorHandler.ts — do 500s leak stack/PII? Check a few catch blocks that res.json(e) raw.\n6. Auth endpoints: /api/auth/* — login/register/OTP responses: user enumeration (different errors for unknown email?), OTP brute force, google sign-in email verification bypass, response payload over-sharing.\n7. Swagger /api/docs — openapi.ts: does it expose internal endpoints or example PII?\n8. Static + (when test-harness note says DB up) dynamic spot-checks via supertest for the top 2-3 leaks.\n\nDELIVERABLES: note 'pii-leak-candidates' (findings) prioritized with file:line; record_coverage per surface ('public endpoints PII'); no create_vulnerability_report (reporting agents handle).",
