        "task": "Audit raw SQL and injection sinks in /workspace/server (call get_threat_model target /workspace/server first).\n\nSHELL QUIRK: exec_command default pipes swallow output — always pass tty:true.\n\nDO:\n1. rg for '\\$queryRaw|\\$executeRaw|queryRawUnsafe|executeRawUnsafe' across src/ — for EACH hit, determine whether any part of the SQL string is built from user input (params, query strings, sort/order/filter fields, table names). Prisma tagged-template $queryRaw\\`...\\` is parameterized ONLY for interpolated VALUES via Prisma.sql/Prisma.join — string concatenation inside the template or $raw string args are injectable. Document each with file:line and attacker-controlled reachability (which route/param reaches it).\n2. utils/list.ts parseListParams: does sort/order flow into prisma orderBy as raw field name? Prisma orderBy is NOT SQL but unknown-field errors can leak schema; worse if any list route passes sort into raw SQL. Check setListHeaders and all callers of parseListParams.\n3. Check admin.routes.ts raw queries (metrics ~line 478) for interpolated filters (search terms from admin UI).\n4. Check prisma/seed.ts and scripts/ for injection only if reachable via app routes (skip otherwise).\n5. Non-SQL injection quick sweep while you're there: child_process usage (exec/execSync) with user input, path traversal in file serving (utils/storage.ts resolveExamFile/resolvePatientPhoto, admin upload endpoints, data.routes.ts export/import), template injection, command injection in extraction pipeline.\n6. For each candidate: trace source (route param/body) → sink. For non-obviously-reachable ones mark open gap. \n7. Dynamic validation when the 'test-harness' note says Postgres is up: build /workspace/server/test/poc-sqli.test.ts with supertest hitting the reachable sink with a benign marker payload (e.g. sort=id;SELECT or ' OR '1'='1 via -- where applicable; use time-based only if boolean not observable). Prove or refute. Use resetDb from test/helpers.\n\nDELIVERABLES: note 'sqli-injection-candidates' (findings) with file:line + reachability + PoC result; record_coverage per sink surface; NO create_vulnerability_report (reporting agents file).",
